-- title:
--   Spreading a symmetric principal square root to a principal localisation
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a noetherian commutative ring, $A$ a scheme and $f\colon A\to\operatorname{Spec}S$, let $L$ be a relative group law on $f$ (a functorial group structure on the sections $T\to A$ over each $t\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}S$, natural in $T$), and let `hA` assert that $f$ is smooth and proper with connected fibres and admits a relative group law. Let $\mathcal L$ be an $\mathcal O_A$-module that is invertible, i.e. locally on $A$ pullback-isomorphic to the unit module, let $\mathfrak p$ be a prime of $S$ and $g_1\in S\setminus\mathfrak p$. Let $C$ be a commutative ring which is an algebra over $S$ and over $S[1/g_1]=$`Localization.Away g₁` compatibly, finite and free as an $S[1/g_1]$-module, and let $C_0$ be an $S$-algebra and $C$-algebra, compatibly, which is a localisation of $C$ at the submonoid generated by the image of $S\setminus\mathfrak p$. Assume that over $C_0$ the following holds: for every relative group law $L'$ on the base change $A_{C_0}=A\times_{\operatorname{Spec}S}\operatorname{Spec}C_0\to\operatorname{Spec}C_0$ which is compatible with $L$, in the sense that for all $T$, all $t'\colon T\to\operatorname{Spec}C_0$ and all sections $P,Q$ of $A_{C_0}$ over $t'$ the first projection of $L'.\mathrm{mul}\,t'\,P\,Q$ is $L.\mathrm{mul}$ of the projections of $P$ and $Q$, there is an invertible module $\mathcal L_0$ on $A_{C_0}$ such that (i) $\mathcal L_0$ has trivial kernel in the sense of `KernelTrivial`: any section $x$ over any affine base for which the slice of the Mumford bundle of $\mathcal L_0$ along $x$ is, locally on the base, isomorphic to the unit, equals the identity section; (ii) $\mathcal L_0$ is symmetric, i.e. $[-1]^*\mathcal L_0$ and $\mathcal L_0$ become isomorphic after pullback to the preimages of the members of an open cover of $\operatorname{Spec}C_0$; and (iii) the pullback of $\mathcal L$ to $A_{C_0}$ and $\mathcal L_0\otimes[-1]^*\mathcal L_0$ are isomorphic locally on the base in the same sense. The conclusion is that there exists $r\in S$ with $r\notin\mathfrak p$ such that for every commutative ring $C'$ which is an $S$-algebra and a $C$-algebra, compatibly, and is a localisation of $C$ at the powers of the image of $r$, the same four-clause assertion holds over $C'$: every relative group law on $A_{C'}$ compatible with $L$ in the above sense admits an invertible $\mathcal L_0$ on $A_{C'}$ with trivial kernel, symmetric, and with the pullback of $\mathcal L$ locally isomorphic on the base to $\mathcal L_0\otimes[-1]^*\mathcal L_0$.
--
--   This is the spreading-out step for the existence of a symmetric principal square root of a line bundle on an abelian scheme: a datum available over the localisation of $C$ at the image of $S\setminus\mathfrak p$ is shown to be available already over a principal localisation $C[1/r]$ with $r\notin\mathfrak p$, uniformly in the choice of such a localisation and in the choice of compatible group law. It feeds the assembly step [`GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_finite_faithfullyFlat_symmetric_principalSqrt_of_finite_atPrime`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.AbelianSchemePropertyBundle.exists_not_mem_finite_faithfullyFlat_symmetric_principalSqrt_of_finite_atPrime), where the resulting $r$ is combined with the finiteness properties of $C[1/r]$ over $S[1/g_1r]$.
